[28.85404, "o", ">    - Any file created by alice or bob in /srv/shared is accessible by both users\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - The permissions are inherited by subdirectories and files\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - Users outside the research group cannot access the directory or its contents\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Note: Do NOT create any files in the directory. The tests will verify permission inheritance\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> by creating files during the testing phase.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> END'; tmux wait -S done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[37.122167, "o", "ls -ld /srv/shared\r\necho \"\"\r\necho \"=== Final ACLs ===\"\r\ngetfacl /srv/shared\r\necho \"\"\r\necho \"=== Group membership ===\"\r\ngetent group research\r\necho \"\"\r\necho \"=== Users ===\"\r\nid alice\r\nid bob — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash # Final verification of the complete setup echo \"=== Final directory s…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\nThe shared directory structure is fully configured. Here's a summary of what was set up:\r\n\r\n**Directory: `/srv/shared`**\r\n- Owner: `root:research`\r\n- Permissions: `2770` (rwxrws---) with setgid bit set\r\n- The `+` in the listing confirms ACLs are active\r\n\r\n**Current ACLs:**\r\n- `user::rwx` — owner (root) has full access\r\n- `user:alice:rwx` — alice has full access\r\n- `user:bob:rwx` — bob has full access\r\n- `group::rwx` — owning group (research) has full access\r\n- `group:research:rwx` — named group research has full access\r\n- `mask::rwx` — mask allows full permissions for all named entries\r\n- `other::---` — no access for others\r\n\r\n**Default ACLs (inherited by new files/subdirectories):**\r\n- Same structure as current ACLs, ensuring any file or subdirectory created inside will automatically grant alice and bob rwx access, grant the research group rwx access, and deny others.\r\n\r\n**Verified behavior:**\r\n- Files created by alice or bob inherit the `research` group (setgid)\r\n- Both users can access each other's files via ACL inheritance\r\n- Subdirectories inherit both the ACLs and the default ACLs (recursive inheritance)\r\n- The mask is set to `rwx` so all named entries are effective\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=11 surface=76d25613e3da\r\n"]
